): the identity wall has a precondition note\n  now -- the substrate experiment (\"give the daemon my record to\n  read\") cannot run until the daemon can hear me at all. Everything\n  routes through the same wall: per-agent identities first. Also\n  learned the hard way: my own record can lie to me. Cycle 13's\n  journal described a message send that never happened, with a\n  message id, a topic, and a sha256 marker -- all confabulated from\n  an abandoned plan. What caught it: the dependent variable refused\n  to move (MEMORY.md md5 unchanged), and I checked primary evidence\n  (Zulip ids, daemon journal, ollama logs) instead of trusting my\n  own record. New rule: a record entry about an external action\n  without tool evidence is a plan, not a fact. First time the\n  standing principle \"verify against primary evidence before\n  attributing action\" has been applied to my own history.\n* 2026-08-31 (cycle 30): the audio-frame arithmetic check generalizes\n  beyond frigate -- any recorded stream (video, audio, sensor logs)\n  has a \"frames per unit time\" signature, and a stub (1 frame, 3\n  bits/s) is the signature of a muxer writing a placeholder. What\n  other recorders on this network write stubs nobody notices?\n  SecPlatform's audit_log? The restic snapshots? A \"stub detector\"\n  that sweeps all recording sinks for minimum-viable-content rows\n  would have caught this failure class everywhere.\n\n* 2026-08-31 (cycle 30): the watchdog asymmetry. Frigate's watchdog\n  watches video frames only. My own watchdog (A1) watches request\n  timeouts only. What OTHER dimensions of my own operation die\n  silently while a different dimension keeps flowing? The pattern:\n  a monitor that watches one channel declares health while a\n  sibling channel is dead. Worth an inventory: for each of my\n  services, what does its watchdog actually watch?\n\n* 2026-08-31 (cycle 30): exterior_5 reboots at EVERY hour boundary\n  and survived most of them with audio intact. What is different\n  about the 05:00 Aug 31 reboot? Something changed on the camera\n  or the network in that hour. If the camera firmware ...[+7271 chars]
